WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.123
This ERD shows the logical blueprint for the clinic
Patient and provider

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:11.297
each connect to appointment Appointment then
connects to service through the appointment

00:00:11.323 --> 00:00:16.974
service junction table Read each relationship
separately rather than trying

00:00:16.987 --> 00:00:22.505
to understand the entire diagram at once Patient to
appointment is

00:00:22.531 --> 00:00:28.034
one-to-many Provider to appointment is one-to-many
Appointment to

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:33.812
service is many-to-many so appointment service sits
between them Notice

00:00:33.839 --> 00:00:38.115
that appointment service also stores facts about the
relationship such as quantity

00:00:38.141 --> 00:00:42.710
and unit charge Those values do not belong only to
the appointment

00:00:42.736 --> 00:00:47.236
or only to the service They belong to the specific
service used

00:00:47.249 --> 00:00:52.748
in a specific appointment That is one reason
junction tables are often

00:00:52.762 --> 00:00:55.854
real business entities rather than only technical
connectors
